   <p style="margin: 0pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify;">The fair values of these mortgage servicing rights were $<ix:nonFraction id="c148439567" contextRef="i_2026-06-30" unitRef="USD" name="ebmt:MortgageServicingRightsMeasuredAtFairValue" scale="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="INF">19,815,000</ix:nonFraction>&#160;and $<ix:nonFraction id="c148439568" contextRef="i_2025-12-31" unitRef="USD" name="ebmt:MortgageServicingRightsMeasuredAtFairValue" scale="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="INF">20,302,000</ix:nonFraction> at&#160;<em style="font: inherit;"> June 30, 2026</em>&#160;and&#160;<em style="font: inherit;"> December 31, 2025</em>, respectively. The fair value of mortgage servicing rights was determined at loan level, depending on the interest rate and term of the specific loan, using the following valuation assumptions:</p>
