  <p style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; margin: 0pt;">&#160;</p>
  <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify;">Net Interest Margin ("NIM"). Net interest margin for the three months&#160;ended June 30, 2026&#160;was 4.15<span style="background-color:#ffffff;">%, an increase of 24&#160;basis points&#160;compared to the three months ended&#160;June 30, 2025.</span>&#160;Net interest margin for the six&#160;months&#160;ended June 30, 2026&#160;was 4.13<span style="background-color:#ffffff">%, an increase of 31&#160;basis points&#160;compared to the six&#160;months ended&#160;June 30, 2025.</span>The increase in NIM reflects lower funding costs and improved balance sheet leverage through a favorable funding mix&#160;and reduced borrowings, with stable yields on interest&#8209;earning assets.</p>
  <p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: left">&#160;</p>
